# sweep-world-gpu.steps -- the 3D world through the SDL_GPU backend (-gpu)
# against GL (#340 P2b): the world, brush entities, alias models (the
# viewmodel) and the classic scrolling sky, on retail demo1.
#
# Run the SAME binary both ways, with identical settings:
#
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 +map demo1"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/w-gl  ~/hexen2 $A
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd json> STEPS=tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/w-gpu ~/hexen2 -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 $A
#
# then the three checks:
#
#   1. GL against -gpu, every frame:
#        PSNR_MIN=40 ./tools/shot-diff.sh /tmp/w-gl /tmp/w-gpu 200x24+100+576
#   2. Front faces: -gpu with culling on (0x) draws what -gpu with it off (1x)
#      draws, bar the handful of pixels GL's own pair differs by (back faces
#      peeking through at silhouettes): AE under 240 (0.05%) per pair:
#        for f in /tmp/w-gpu/1*.png; do b=$(basename $f); \
#          magick compare -metric AE /tmp/w-gpu/0${b#1} $f null:; echo " $b"; done
#      Were rg_pipeline.c's front face inverted, gl_cull 1 would cull every
#      wall the camera faces -- the world (already backface-culled on the CPU)
#      goes blank and only some alias models remain.  This pair cannot see a
#      backend that ignored culling altogether; check 1 does.
#   3. The world frame reached nothing unrouted: between REPORT-WORLD-BEGIN and
#      REPORT-WORLD-END in /tmp/w-gpu/qconsole.log, gpu_unrouted lists no
#      glDrawElements*, glBindVertexArray, glVertexAttrib4f or glClear, and
#      renderer_status reports the segments per frame.
#
# With the Vulkan validation layers on (VK_LAYER_PATH=<vulkan-validation-layers>
# /share/vulkan/explicit_layer.d, +gpu_debug 1) the -gpu run must log no
# "Validation Error".
#
# The settings below turn off what -gpu does not draw yet, on BOTH sides, so
# the comparison is of the same draw paths: the post-process chain (gamma 1 on
# the command line, r_bloom, r_ssao: P4), compute and storage-buffer lighting
# (r_gpulightstyles, r_dlight_occlusion, r_dynamic: P5), alias instancing
# (r_alias_gpu: needs shader storage, P2e -- off here so GL draws the CPU path
# -gpu takes), particles (P3, and random), fog (P3), MSAA (-fsaa 0: P6),
# anisotropic filtering (GL_Init_NullGL leaves gl_max_anisotropy at 1).  The
# rest make a frame repeatable: setpos cameras (a timed turn lands on a
# different yaw each run, see sweep-worldcull.steps), the game paused before
# each shot, flat lightstyles, a still sky (it scrolls with realtime, which a
# pause does not stop), and no crosshair.
#
# The 200x24+100+576 mask is the mini status bar's health: the player takes a
# knock at spawn before god is on, by a run-dependent amount.
#
# THE THRESHOLD.  shot-diff.sh's header: a gate calibrated on one lucky pair
# is worthless, so it comes from three runs.  Measured 2026-11-19, 800x600,
# llvmpipe GL against lavapipe -gpu (Mesa 26.2), PSNR in dB, masked:
#
#   camera          GL vs -gpu, runs 1/2/3    GL vs GL    -gpu vs -gpu
#   01-statue-sky   50.52  50.47  50.70       62.1 64.1   61.6 identical
#   02-arch         51.51  51.51  51.51       identical   identical
#   03-tree         51.36  51.36  51.36       identical   identical
#   04-cross        52.47  52.47  52.47       identical   identical
#   05-wall         51.76  51.76  51.76       identical   identical
#   06-courtyard    52.30  52.30  52.30       identical   identical
#   11..16          49.13 (11) .. 52.47       53.5 on 11  56.9 on 11
#
# (01 and 11 hold a spinning pickup, which a pause catches at a run-dependent
# angle.)  The broken builds the gate exists for, same cameras: front face
# inverted 19.2-24.9 dB, clear depth 1.0 or gl_clipcontrol_able left false
# 17.8-22.3 dB, the world VBO built under -gpu (world not drawn) 19.7-26.6
# dB.  So 40 dB: 9 dB under the worst honest camera, 13 dB over the best
# broken one.  Culling: -gpu 0x vs 1x differs by 9-38 pixels, GL's pair by
# 9-44; the inverted front face by 23,868-47,236.
#
# llvmpipe and lavapipe share Mesa's rasterizer.  On a Tesla P4 (NVIDIA
# Vulkan) against the same llvmpipe GL frames taken with anisotropic
# filtering still on, the cameras read 39.9-45.2 dB: the 40 dB gate is for
# the Mesa pair, and a hardware pair needs its own three runs.

sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 0
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
sleep 2

# --- culling on (gl_cull 1, the default) ---
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 -20 45 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 01-statue-sky
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 135 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 02-arch
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 225 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 03-tree
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 315 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 04-cross
cmd pause
cmd setpos -700 -1700 0 -10 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 05-wall
cmd pause
cmd setpos -1100 -1800 100 -30 0 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 06-courtyard
cmd pause

# --- the world frame's unrouted calls, on the last camera ---
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
sleep 2
cmd echo REPORT-WORLD-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-WORLD-END
sleep 1

# --- culling off: the same cameras ---
cmd gl_cull 0
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 -20 45 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 11-statue-sky
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 135 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 12-arch
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 225 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 13-tree
cmd pause
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 0 315 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 14-cross
cmd pause
cmd setpos -700 -1700 0 -10 90 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 15-wall
cmd pause
cmd setpos -1100 -1800 100 -30 0 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 16-courtyard
cmd pause
cmd gl_cull 1

# --- r_shadows (#340 P2c): the projected blob shadows test stencil EQUAL 1
# under compare mask 2 and INCR on pass, so each pixel darkens at most twice;
# under -gpu that needs the stencil and the compare mask in the pipeline key.
# Same camera as 01, which holds a pickup.  Measured 2026-11-19 as the rest:
# GL vs -gpu 49.0 / 50.1 / 51.5 dB, GL vs GL 55.6 / 49.7, Tesla P4 48.1.  The
# blob is small, so this camera checks that the stencil-tested shadow
# pipelines build and draw without a validation error more than it checks
# the stencil arithmetic: the P2b binary, which draws the shadow unmasked,
# also passes it (48.9 dB).
cmd r_shadows 1
cmd setpos -918 -2034 0 -20 45 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 21-shadows
cmd pause
cmd r_shadows 0
